# Secrets. tools/.env holds the NCBI API key and must never be published.
# tools/.env.example is tracked, so a collaborator knows what to create.
.env

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Copyrighted source articles. writing_guides/writing_rules.md is the distilled
# digest, it is tracked, and per CLAUDE.md it is what drafting actually loads.
# The source PDFs are not read by any code - they are cited in comments as the
# source of a measurement - and are not ours to redistribute.
#
# As of 2026-09-24 they are not in this tree at all: they live in the sibling
# `paper-engine-corpus/writing_guides/`, so the repository tree is only what a
# member receives. The rule stays so that dropping one back in here is still
# ignored rather than committed by accident.
writing_guides/*.pdf

# OneDrive and Windows noise
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
*~
*.tmp

# Word lock files, created while a .docx is open
~$*.docx

# The report spool. On a source checkout this is where defect records wait to
# be sent, and where report.json keeps the reports-repo token - so it is a
# secret directory, not just noise. Members installing the plugin never use
# this path at all; theirs resolves to ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA}. See
# specs/distribution.md 5.
.spool/

# The probe corpus: real, unpublished manuscripts, with a real byline and a
# real email in them. `specs/flow-and-conclusion-2026-09-19.md`,
# `specs/probes/sentence-boundary-2026-09-20/` and
# `specs/probes/magnitude-2026-09-20/` all read these, and the probes still
# run - the files are on the machine, they are just not in the history.
#
# Kept out because git history is the one place a decision is expensive to
# undo. TODO.md 5.5 is still open on whether this repository goes public, and
# committing somebody's unpublished draft turns that question into a history
# rewrite before it can even be asked. A probe corpus is reproducible; a
# published draft is not retractable.
#
# As of 2026-09-24 the corpus is not in this tree at all: it lives in the
# sibling `paper-engine-corpus/training/`, and both probes resolve it through
# $PAPER_ENGINE_CORPUS, then that sibling, then this path. The rule stays so
# that dropping a draft back in here is still ignored rather than committed.
training/

# The maintainer's notes and the defect ledger stay on the machine that wrote
# them. They are written against real, often unpublished projects, and this
# repository is public. The ledger is created from
# tools/system-changes.template.md on first use.
system-changes.md
specs/
history/
TODO.md
